\chi_{fs}(\alpha)=\frac{\alpha}{\alpha^{2}+\cosh^{2}\alpha}
        =\frac{kh}{(kh)^{2}+\cosh^{2}kh},
\]
so that with the conventional $\rho\equiv\Delta\rho$
$e_{s}^{fs}=\chi_{fs}S_{0}/\Delta\rho g$, $\chi_{fs}\simeq\alpha$
for $\alpha\ll1$ and $\chi_{fs}(1)\approx0.30$.  The $\cosh\alpha$
numerator retained above is the one obtained with the top conditions
as stated, $u_{x}(0)=0$, $\sigma_{zz}(0)=\rho g e$, $\,B(0)=B'(0)=0$,
with no extra $\sigma_{xz}(0)=0$ imposed.  Up to the conventional
$\rho\leftrightarrow\Delta\rho$ identification this is the $O(1)$
geometrical factor normally quoted for viscous dynamic topography. ∎
